# LLM assistant

Optional in-browser coach. No app backend — the browser calls the user’s provider with their key (or builds search links).

## Where it appears

- UI: `LlmAssistantPanel.svelte` — compact editor chrome (**Check (AI)** + **Configure model**)
  - `PracticeIDE` / `SimulationIDE`: `IDEWorkspace` slot `editor-chrome` above Monaco
  - `DsaPracticeIDE` / `QuestionBankIDE`: inside `editor-frame` above `CodeEditor` (reading answers: under the answer box)
- Settings store: `src/lib/stores/llm.js` → localStorage `system-design-copilot-llm-v1`
- Providers + HTTP builders: `src/lib/llm/providers.js`
- Check / outline prompt builders: `src/lib/llm/checkPrompts.js` (`buildAnswerCheckPrompt`)

## Built-in providers

`search-engine`, `openai`, `azure-openai`, `gemini`, `anthropic`, `ollama`, `lm-studio`, `comfyui`, `custom`

Default provider preset (new installs / reset): **search-engine**. Cloud API keys show an in-panel warning; keys stay in browser localStorage only. Search-engine mode builds DuckDuckGo/Google/Perplexity links (no API key).

## Check (AI)

- Primary action on the panel; disabled when the answer draft is empty.
- Prompt always labels **Question:** and **User answer:** plus optional Context lines.
- Flow-specific rubrics for `high-level-design`, `low-level-design`, `data-structures-and-algorithms`, `ai-engineer`, `interview-questions`, and `simulation`.
- Same invocation path as before: `requestLlmCompletion()` or `buildSearchEngineUrls()`.

## API surface

- `buildRequest()`, `requestLlmCompletion()`, `buildSearchEngineUrls()`
- `buildAnswerCheckPrompt()`, `getCheckInstruction()`, `getModeInstruction()`
- Panel holds templates / system prompt from store; hosts pass `flowId`, `objective` (question), `draft` (answer), `contextSections`
- Replies rendered with `markdown-it`

## Agent notes

- Rest of the app must work with LLM unset — never require a key for core lesson/practice flows (search-engine is the zero-key path).
- Keys stay client-side only; do not add a proxy without an explicit product decision.
- Tests: `tests/editorAndLlm.test.js`.
